{
  "about": [
    "Hand-worked TypeSafe report cases. tests/lib/typesafe-report.test.ts gives them to summarizeTypeSafe in lib/typesafe/report.ts, and the tests of rust-api/server/src/typesafe.rs give them to summarize. Both must give the expected counts.",
    "Each evaluation names one of the snapshots below. A field that an evaluation or a decision does not give is null (false for the two decision flags). A time is UTC.",
    "The expected counts are in the order in which the summary first adds each key; the tests compare the JSON text, so the order and a NaN count (written as null) must also agree.",
    "A case with \"error\": true has a snapshot that the summary cannot read: TypeScript throws a TypeError and Rust returns an error."
